      "about_title": "About SUIJI",
      "about_lead": "From custom work to personal combinations.",
      "about_body": "Our designs have grown out of how people really want to wear them. Meet Chunyu Wen and discover how custom-jewelry experience led to a system of bases and charms, with personal choice at its heart.",
      "about_cta": "Meet the designer",
      "editorial_title": "Ways to wear. Things to know.",
      "editorial_body": "What is included? How do you check the fit? Find practical guides to choosing, combining and caring for your jewelry."
    },
    "about": {
      "title": "Jewelry that changes with you.",
      "lead": "Since 2014, our work in handmade jewelry has been shaped by conversations with the people who wear it. SUIJI grew from a wish we heard often: to keep a design you love and find more ways to wear it.",
      "structure_title": "An ornament. A base. Your expression.",
      "structure_body": "In our custom work, some customers wanted a favorite charm to appear in matching earrings, a ring or a necklace. Others wanted to change a detail for a different outfit or occasion. Buying a whole new piece each time often meant buying the same parts again. That experience led us to a modular approach: keep the base you love, choose another compatible charm, or carry a favorite detail across different clasp-equipped bases. The pieces can work together without making you start again with every new idea.",
      "structure_cta": "Explore the SUIJI system",
      "style_title": "From minimal to bold",
      "style_body": "Clean shapes and considered details can stand alone or form a more expressive composition. Proportion, color and material connect the elements; you decide the finished look.",
      "designer_title": "Meet the designer",
      "designer_name": "Chunyu Wen",
      "designer_role": "Founder · Brand & Product Lead",
      "designer_bio": "Chunyu brings her background in bespoke fine jewelry to SUIJI’s brand and product direction, structural development, design and supply chain. She studied Visual Communication at Tsinghua University’s Academy of Arts & Design and Brand Management at INSEEC in France.",
      "designer_approach": "Her work begins with the relationship between an ornament and the structure that makes it wearable, leaving the final expression to the person who wears it.",
      "designer_alt": "Chunyu Wen, founder and designer at SUIJI",
      "wear_title": "Designed to be worn",
      "wear_body": "We use titanium alloy for the parts designed to sit against the skin. Other materials are chosen to suit the design and the way each piece is made, with lightness guiding every choice. We consider how the complete piece feels on the body, as well as how it looks.",
      "team_title": "Product, content and commerce",
      "team_body": "Chunyu leads the brand and product work. Yue Wang, Partner in AI Automation & Marketing, connects product information, content and commerce. Human review remains essential in design, production, quality control and publication.",
      "future_title": "A future shaped by you",
      "future_body": "We are working toward a future where everyone can wear jewelry they have had a hand in designing. SUIJI provides the structure; your ideas, choices and personal connections give each composition its character.",
      "planned": "A service in preparation",
      "planned_body": "Share your style preferences and explore an ornament of your own. SUIJI would check structural fit and production feasibility before the design, price and timing are confirmed. This personal-design service is planned; it is not an ordering tool on this site.",
      "collection_cta": "Explore the collection",
      "sets_cta": "Find your starting point",
      "contact_cta": "Contact SUIJI"
    },
